{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/156162-can-the-gentry-be-used-in-without-a-gmc-update-in-a-post-gmc-game-of-another-line","id":156162,"title":"Can the Gentry be used in without a GMC update in a post GMC game of another line?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-01T19:52:20-07:00","id":156162,"title":"Can the Gentry be used in without a GMC update in a post GMC game of another line?","content":"I like Changeling and I like Blood and Smoke. I like contrast of the Vamps who backstab at the drop of a hat vs the Changelings who keep their word even some arbitrary and strange situations.<br /> But we have to wait for a Changeling update. So I was thinking of using some low power Gentry Actors and Wisps in a Blood &amp; Smoke game to bring that element until we get some post GMC rules for Lost. Any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T20:13:20-07:00","id":156186,"title":"","content":"I don't see why not. A handful of Contracts, such as the Contracts of Lucidity, would probably require tweaking or overhaul, but the nWoD 2e rules are pretty backwards compatible with most systems that don't hook into the Morality tree or derangements, and since the Gentry usually don't track Morality, that's usually not a problem for them. When building Wisps, I'd probably gauge around 5 experiences to spend per dot of Wyrd past the first, charging 2 or 3 experiences for a Contract dot. Virtues and Vices becoming more flexible should serve the Others and their titles well. The Immortal Flesh power should probably get a small boost considering the increased ease of inflicting lethal damage in the second edition rules; maybe give them a couple points of armor against nonmagical attacks without iron weapons, nothing too great. Or just have them take reduce lethal damage without iron to bashing like the Kindred do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T20:39:45-07:00","id":156212,"title":"","content":"Really the issue is that Contracts are a lot weaker than B&amp;S vampire disciplines on a whole. So You'll have to tweak it on a whole if you want a challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T21:47:24-07:00","id":156247,"title":"","content":"Or just give 'em a bunch more of 'em. NPCs and all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T06:58:27-07:00","id":156461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/156162-can-the-gentry-be-used-in-without-a-gmc-update-in-a-post-gmc-game-of-another-line?p=156212#post156212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really the issue is that Contracts are a lot weaker than B&amp;S vampire disciplines on a whole. So You'll have to tweak it on a whole if you want a challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even before Blood and Smoke contracts weren't direct comparisons to disciplines. However they were more a sideways threat if you get my meaning. A cleaver changeling could be a problem. But your right they may need to be beefed up a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T11:39:39-07:00","id":156776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/156162-can-the-gentry-be-used-in-without-a-gmc-update-in-a-post-gmc-game-of-another-line?p=156461#post156461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even before Blood and Smoke contracts weren't direct comparisons to disciplines. However they were more a sideways threat if you get my meaning. A cleaver changeling could be a problem. But your right they may need to be beefed up a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of them. Were others weren't. Really this is my personal issue with contracts Elements 5 is worth a lot more than Talon or ( more laughably) Den 5. I don't think you'll need to change Stone 5 but others could prove an issue. Elements might also be something to look into because 5 is technically 2 agg per turn that they can't do anything about without twilight powers or having an aquarium on hand. It might just be better for times sake to just make up a small set of powers than looking and changing every contract.<br /> <br /> Dice wise though, Actors are incredibly potent as are props. If you are dealing with a 3-title actor he'll have 8/9 in primary stats, 7 to 6 in secondary, and at least 4 to tertiary. With skills ranging at about the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-02-2014, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}